                                "sense_id": "22630d21-e3e8-34bb-a43c-e5ae1e2a6185",
                                "text": "He was speedily reassured, and with a large, white, rascally grin, and a glance at his charge, seemed to take me into partnership in his exalted trust."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6e8ff5b0-d885-4c31-a9e4-4a66c6397c9d",
                                "sense_id": "22630d21-e3e8-34bb-a43c-e5ae1e2a6185",
                                "text": "My chief creditor is, unhappily, my most bitter enemy—a rascally fellow, Sam Brewer, whom I was once compelled to horse-whip on Newmarket Heath."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
